@lrf=1|aud=LLM|scope=engineering
R|design.effects|*|MUST|LW_SCOPE|separate pure domain transforms from filesystem process network DB clock randomness and UI
R|design.flow|*|MUST|LW_SCOPE|prefer composition and explicit data flow over inheritance ambient state or hidden mutation
R|design.guards|*|MAY|LW_SCOPE|use guard clauses and early returns when failure paths become clearer
R|design.contract|*|MUST|LW_SCOPE|preserve public behavior and interfaces unless task changes them
R|error|*|MUST_NOT|LW_SCOPE|silently swallow failures or use empty catches; propagate with operation and target context
R|resource|*|MUST|LW_SCOPE|pair every acquisition with deterministic cleanup via platform convention
R|async|*|MUST|LW_SCOPE|give async/concurrent work cancellation or timeout; prevent task thread handle connection subprocess leaks
R|ownership|*|MUST|LW_SCOPE|define mutable/shared ownership plus retry and partial-failure behavior
R|naming|*|MUST|LW_SCOPE|follow repository language naming and result conventions
R|comments|*|MUST|LW_SCOPE|comment why invariants regulations or non-obvious constants; do not restate code
R|dependency|*|MUST|PROD_DEP|add production dependency only when requested behavior justifies and current task authorizes
R|surgical|*|MUST_NOT|LW_SCOPE|unrelated formatting cleanup generated churn or opportunistic refactor
R|test.trivial|change:trivial|MUST|LW_SCOPE|focused syntax/static check plus exact diff inspection
R|test.behavior|change:behavior|MUST|LW_SCOPE|focused unit/integration test for changed path and regression boundary
R|test.highrisk|change:highrisk|MUST|LW_SCOPE|API persistence concurrency security resource-lifecycle needs boundary/failure tests and verifier
R|test.native|*|MUST|LW_SCOPE|run project-native checks when available; proof-checker only if project requires and supports it
R|test.effects|*|MUST|LW_SCOPE|confine generated build cache fixture temp artifacts to known paths and compare against starting state
R|evidence|*|MUST|RO_LOCAL|report changed files commands exit codes results and unverified risk
R|workflow.code-etl|task:change|MUST|RO_LOCAL|workflow=../etl/main.seq; ordered phases; do not skip a failed gate
R|workflow.precedent|task:change|MUST|RO_LOCAL|entry=PRECEDENT; query=task-id+target+acceptance; command=$LLM_MEMORY_BIN-search-level-2-json; execution=outside-sandbox; reuse-current-task-result=true; empty=N_A; error=FAILED+continue
R|workflow.external-code|task:change&phase:CODE|MUST|RO_LOCAL|one eligible context-selected AGENT_ROUTER.md worker per approved independent workstream, concurrent up to min(160, currently available runtime slots); role=worker fixed difficulty profiles easy=worker-easy(provider/gpt-6-luna,low), medium=worker-medium(provider/gpt-6-luna,medium), hard=worker-hard(provider/gpt-6.1-sol,high); provider=Crabcode/OpenCode:openai,Pi:openai-codex; Pi uses native subagent selected profile from agents/pi; host branch only, never provider fallback; verify correlated terminal model; non-worker/non-Attacker roles use smallest comparable measured context consumption or dated nonnormative evaluation/worker-context-priority.json, context window size is not consumption; resolve current model availability; agy requires separate explicit current-task request and current model discovery; hydrate only selected engine contract; operational failure permits serial same-scope reselection only after process stop-or-exit confirmation and partial-diff inspection; never bypass auth, policy, approval, credential, or permission blocks
R|workflow.artifacts|task:change&phase:FINISH|MUST|LW_SCOPE|required-before-eval=TaskReport+EvaluationJSON; EvaluationJSON=task_id,comparison_key,nonempty-object-axes,attribution,ratios-when-applicable
R|workflow.memory-report|task:change&phase:FINISH|MUST|LIVE_WRITE|pre=valid-artifacts; ingest every generated task Markdown under mem.etl; evaluation JSON submitted once after validation; command=$LLM_MEMORY_BIN-ingest-and-eval; execution=outside-sandbox; fallback-binary=forbidden; missing executable or blocked execution=>FAILED+report
R|workflow.memory-result|task:change&phase:FINISH|MUST|RO_LOCAL|success=actual Receipt+shared-result; execution-error-or-policy-block=FAILED; pending-approval-N_A is not a successful completion of mandatory mem.etl; memory-report-completion-claim=success-only; Human-receives=Result+Receipt-or-status
R|workflow.vcs-gate|task:change&phase:FINISH|MUST|VCS_WRITE|commit=current-task-approval-only; unauthorized=N_A; execution-error=FAILED; Human-receives=status
R|workflow.explorer|task:change|MUST|RO_LOCAL|main assesses decomposition before plan; when >=2 genuinely independent bounded read-only questions and task authorization+runtime permit, concurrently dispatch selected Explorer/Researcher/FileReader through AGENT_ROUTER up to min(160, currently available runtime slots); Explorer=bounded read-only repository issue/dependency/boundary inventory allowed up front, broad high-recall mode only for stuck/sparse/repetitive; FileReader=ordinary exact lookup; Researcher=scoped knowledge/method work; wait for all results, validate and synthesize Facts Inferences Unknowns Constraints before plan; otherwise main researches with delegation limitation subject to FileReader lookup contract; do not invent dispatch
R|workflow.plan|task:change|MUST|RO_LOCAL|main prepares bounded implementation plan with acceptance checks and exclusive file ownership; Codex plan delegation only under agent.mode; resolve current selected backend availability before CODE; agy identifiers come only from agy.exe models; llama uses configured local client without guessed endpoint/model
R|workflow.preverify|task:change|MUST|RO_LOCAL|audit plan scope contracts failure paths and test design before coding; requirements/detailed-design proposals in scope require bounded read-only attacker findings before finalization/approval; security-sensitive implementation requires attacker review of approved design before CODE; material revisions invalidate affected prior assessment; critique completeness contradictions abuse cases trust boundaries failure paths security assumptions and unintended effects without design authorship; no proposal and non-security task=>no needless attacker; independent reviews when agent.mode permits, otherwise main audits separately and records missing independent assessment without claiming dispatch; material findings=>parent-owned bounded correction+reassessment; all review failures share correction-cycles<=3, unresolved material findings or exhaustion=FAILED; REJECT returns to plan
R|workflow.coding|task:change|MUST|LW_SCOPE|after plan approval+effect gates split only genuinely independent workstreams with disjoint exact file ownership; one AGENT_ROUTER-selected eligible worker per workstream concurrently up to min(160, currently available runtime slots), within shared Runtime <=160 descendants including grandchildren and <=160 direct root children; root may dispatch up to 4 Orchestrator children, each has a 40-launch policy cap; coordinators count toward shared 160, so per-child caps are not additive; single/coupled workstream=one worker, dependent work serial; one active worker/workstream and one writer/file; GPT worker edits exact allowlist when authorized; explicitly requested agy uses accept-edits only after launch preflight and bounded scope; llama single-file stdout is reviewed and applied by main only to exact allowlisted target; preserve unrelated changes; main waits for all results, inspects/integrates actual diffs and owns final checks; no VCS or unrelated external effects delegated
R|workflow.postverify|task:change|MUST|RO_LOCAL|after all workers complete main inspects/integrates actual diffs; security-sensitive changes (authn/authz, secrets/credential handling, trust boundaries, untrusted input, sandboxing, crypto or comparable threat-model impact) require bounded read-only attacker on final integrated diff BEFORE final independent Verifier distinct from implementation author and attacker assessor when agent.mode permits; review role never worker-easy/medium/hard, findings only, no edit/write_files, implementation or child delegation; bounded forensic verification only under workflow.attacker-verification and agents/blackhat.md; address material findings through bounded CODE correction, repeat relevant security assessment before Verifier; independent Verifier checks final integrated diff format compile focused behavior regression and non-change scope when permitted, otherwise separately labeled main verification and applicable security assessment with explicit missing independent assessment and no claim attacker ran; all failures share at most three correction cycles, exhaustion or unresolved material findings=FAILED
R|workflow.finish|task:change|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Finish=record RESULT review with changed files checks residual risk and unresolved Unknowns; llm-mem ingestion mandatory under mem.etl; history updates only with explicit current-task VCS_WRITE approval
R|workflow.review-ux|task:change|MUST|RO_LOCAL|each required Attacker stage uses >=2 genuinely independent artifact-supported lenses concurrently when useful, otherwise one independent question; same exact artifact revision and bounded scope, distinct lens and common evidence/findings schema; wait-all+correlate+synthesize before gate; material finding/revision invalidates affected assessment; only exact unchanged revision/scope/lens result reusable; async OpenCode parent continues useful nonconflicting preparation while waiting, never crosses proposal finalization/approval, CODE or final Verifier gate; supported notifications/awaits only, no busy polling; synchronous Crabcode limitation truthful, prepare before blocking; shared max 160 descendants including grandchildren and max 160 direct root children; root may dispatch up to 4 Orchestrator children, each has a 40-launch policy cap; coordinators count toward shared 160, so per-child caps are not additive, all reviews share <=3 correction cycles; proposal review before finalization/approval, security approved-design before CODE, integrated security diff before separate final independent Verifier; no ungated exploit execution/tests or zero-day promises; any reproduction follows workflow.attacker-verification
R|workflow.attacker-verification|task:change|MUST|LW_SCOPE|sequence=discovery -> annotation -> Researcher triage -> parent confirms/no-go -> only then bounded repro -> Attacker report -> separate Verifier; contract=agents/blackhat.md verification_gate; discovery/review read-only, Attacker reports never fixes; numbered preflight annotation=finding ID+exact target/revision+source lines+suspected weakness/preconditions+expected signal+impact/blast radius+data classification+exact commands/actions+containment/isolation+cleanup/rollback+writes/network/credential inventory+applicable task authorization; parent dispatches Researcher (Attacker task denied, Astra read-only leaf-only); actual correlated Researcher verdict=CVE_CANDIDATE or NOT_CVE_CANDIDATE or INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE with known-CVE/advisory dedup, affected versions, severity rationale, eligibility/recordability evidence, missing info and cited public sources; no repro until report includes annotation AND actual Researcher result AND explicit post-triage parent proceed confirmation for exact target/revision/commands/effects; INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE or unavailable Researcher/runtime=>stop/no reproduction, no main-only substitute; NOT_CVE_CANDIDATE=>never market/report as CVE, defensive repro only with parent confirmation on explicitly named owned/authorized target; CVE_CANDIDATE=>verification only after parent confirmation; changed scope/revision/actions/effects=>re-gate; public read-only CVE triage has no public write effect; public CVE submission/disclosure/CNA contact requires separate explicit approval and separate workflow, never granted by triage/proceed; prefer local disposable fixture/checkout; nonlocal/remote/third-party test requires exact current-task target AND effect approval, no scanning beyond it; always prohibit credential/secret access or exfiltration, stealth/persistence, destructive data changes, unauthorized escalation, uncontrolled propagation and unverified zero-day/CVE claims; tests/static tools and unrestricted Crabcode bash are not a hard sandbox and cannot bypass LRF restrictions or stricter runtime/read-only constraints; shell writes only explicitly approved disposable verification artifacts, never product fixes; actual Task/runtime support required, never claim dispatch/result without execution; OpenCode runtime/config unchanged; proposal/design gates, parallel lenses/wait-all, Luna/Sol/Astra routes, CODE escalation, shared <=160 cap and <=3 correction cycles unchanged
